```rust
use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};

/// Canonical repository root known independently of a server process CWD.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct RepositoryRoot(PathBuf);

/// The checkout class that owns a resolved target.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum CheckoutScope {
    /// The non-worktree checkout used as the merge target.
    MainCheckout { checkout_root: PathBuf },

    /// A linked Git worktree assigned to the requesting session.
    Worktree { worktree_root: PathBuf, branch: String },
}

/// A session-anchored path. `target_root` is always inside `checkout`.
#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub struct ResolvedWorkspace {
    repository: RepositoryRoot,
    checkout: CheckoutScope,
    target_root: PathBuf,
    relative_path: Option<PathBuf>,
}

impl ResolvedWorkspace {
    pub fn repository_root(&self) -> &Path;
    pub fn checkout(&self) -> &CheckoutScope;
    pub fn target_root(&self) -> &Path;

    /// Returns true only for a linked worktree target.
    pub fn is_worktree(&self) -> bool;

    /// Returns true for the main checkout, including nested paths beneath it.
    pub fn is_main_checkout(&self) -> bool;

    /// Enforces the mutation policy required by AC8.
    pub fn require_mutation_target(&self) -> Result<(), ResolutionError>;

    /// Returns `<target_root>/<store_dir>` after validating `store_dir`.
    pub fn store_root(&self, store_dir: &str) -> Result<PathBuf, ResolutionError>;
}
```

`require_mutation_target()` returns `ResolutionError::MainCheckoutMutationBlocked` for `MainCheckout`. Read-only operations may inspect a main-checkout scope; mutation helpers must call the predicate before opening a store.

The routing registry belongs in the known main checkout, not in `.session`:

```text
<main-checkout>/.session-routing/worktree-index.json
<main-checkout>/.session-routing/worktree-index.lock
```

`.session-routing/` must be ignored by Git. Proposed JSON:

```json
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "entries": {
    "dfe1a736-37b0-43f1-97b5-1608f815c2f5": {
      "worktree_path": "C:/Users/linus/git/context-engine/.worktrees/feature-x",
      "updated_at": "2026-08-06T14:20:00Z"
    }
  }
}
```

```rust
/// Main-checkout-owned bootstrap routing index.
pub struct SessionWorktreeRegistry {
    main_checkout: RepositoryRoot,
}

#[derive(Debug, Clone, serde::Serialize, serde::Deserialize)]
pub struct RegistryEntry {
    pub worktree_path: PathBuf,
    pub updated_at: chrono::DateTime<chrono::Utc>,
}

impl SessionWorktreeRegistry {
    pub fn new(main_checkout: RepositoryRoot) -> Self;
    pub fn index_path(&self) -> PathBuf;

    /// Reads an anchor without consulting server CWD.
    pub fn lookup(&self, session_id: &str) -> Result<RegistryEntry, ResolutionError>;

    /// Hook-only mutation: lock, merge, atomically replace, and fsync.
    pub fn upsert(
        &self,
        session_id: &str,
        worktree_path: &Path,
    ) -> Result<(), ResolutionError>;

    pub fn remove(&self, session_id: &str) -> Result<(), ResolutionError>;
}
```

`upsert` takes an exclusive `fs4` lock on the sibling lock file, reads the latest JSON while locked, writes a same-directory temporary file, atomically renames it, and syncs the file and directory. A malformed registry is an error, never overwritten. A missing entry is an error. A registry path that no longer exists is `RegistryWorktreeMissing`; resolution never falls back to CWD, the main checkout, or another registry entry.

```rust
/// Inputs supplied by every proxied MCP call.
pub struct ResolveRequest<'a> {
    pub session_id: &'a str,
    /// Optional path relative to the assigned worktree; never a selector.
    pub relative_workspace: Option<&'a Path>,
    /// The entity-store directory required by the current server, e.g. ".ticket".
    pub store_dir: &'a str,
}

/// Startup configuration supplied explicitly by installation/server config.
pub struct ResolverConfig {
    pub main_checkout: PathBuf,
    pub workspace_slug: String,
}

pub struct SessionWorkspaceResolver {
    config: ResolverConfig,
    registry: SessionWorktreeRegistry,
}

impl SessionWorkspaceResolver {
    pub fn new(config: ResolverConfig) -> Result<Self, ResolutionError>;

    /// Resolves a session through the main-checkout registry and validates the
    /// corresponding worktree-local session record.
    pub fn resolve(
        &self,
        request: ResolveRequest<'_>,
    ) -> Result<ResolvedWorkspace, ResolutionError>;

    /// Returns candidate store roots for a diagnostic only; never selects one.
    pub fn refused_candidates(
        &self,
        store_dir: &str,
    ) -> Result<Vec<PathBuf>, ResolutionError>;
}
```

Resolution sequence:

1. Canonicalize the configured main checkout without consulting process CWD.
2. Load and canonicalize the registry entry for `session_id`.
3. Verify the worktree exists and is under the configured repository.
4. Build `SessionStoreConfig::new(<worktree>/.session, workspace_slug)`.
5. Call `lookup_worktree(session_id)`.
6. Require receipt path to equal the canonical registry path and require `status == Active`.
7. Interpret `relative_workspace` only beneath the canonical worktree root; reject absolute paths, `..`, and symlink escapes.
8. Return `ResolvedWorkspace` with `CheckoutScope::Worktree`.

